# Seed for this clone's .git/info/exclude - artifacts left behind by OTHER branches.
#
# What: .git/info/exclude is git's per-clone ignore file (gitignore syntax, never committed, applies
# on every branch, honored by "git status" and "git clean -X", shared by all worktrees of a clone).
# This repository uses it for one job: hiding artifacts that ANOTHER branch of the template family
# leaves in the working tree after a branch switch. That keeps every committed .gitignore describing
# only what its OWN branch produces - a base branch never needs to know descendant structure.
#
# Apply (idempotent; appends only what is missing, never removes):
#     $ node --run setup:git-exclude
# Or by hand: append the patterns below to .git/info/exclude.
#
# Updating: each branch family appends the artifact patterns its layer introduces, next to a short
# comment, so the list stays additive and merges cleanly. This is a convenience seed, not a
# strict-sync file - if a sibling family's pattern is missing here, the cost is one line added
# locally, nothing breaks.
#
# Precedence note: tracked .gitignore files override .git/info/exclude, and within one file the last
# matching line wins - so a pattern + "!" negation pair (like the encryption-keys pair below) works
# here exactly as it would in a .gitignore.

# Frontend build output (config-driven publicDirectory) - frontend-build family
/public-*/

# Local configuration files - web-app family
/config/*.local.js
/config/*.local.secrets.js

# Encryption keys (config/encryption/ on the web-app family; that family guards them via its tracked
# config/encryption/keys/.gitignore - these lines keep leftovers invisible on the other branches)
/config/encryption/keys/*.pem
!/config/encryption/keys/*.documented.runtime.*.pem

# Application data (databases etc.) - web-app family; that family keeps the directory structure
# present via tracked per-directory .gitignore files
/app-data/
